  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A polygon TTT is said to be inside a polygon SSS if all points that lie strictly inside TTT (not on the perimeter of TTT) also lie strictly inside SSS.\n\nA multiset of polygons {Q1,Q2,…,Qr}\\{Q_1, Q_2, \\ldots, Q_r\\}{Q1​,Q2​,…,Qr​} is said to form a chain if there is a permutation p1,p2,…,prp_1, p_2, \\ldots, p_rp1​,p2​,…,pr​ of the integers 111 through rrr such that for each iii (1≤i&lt;r1 \\le i \\lt r1≤i&lt;r), QpiQ_{p_i}Qpi​​ is inside Qpi+1Q_{p_{i+1}}Qpi+1​​.\n\nYou are given NNN convex polygons P1,P2,…,PNP_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_NP1​,P2​,…,PN​ in a 2D Cartesian coordinate system. Every 10−10010^{-100}10−100 seconds, you may choose one of the polygons and translate it by upto 10−10010^{-100}10−100 either along the xxx-axis or along the yyy-axis.\n\nFind the minimum amount of time necessary to make all NNN polygons form a chain or decide that it is impossible.",
    "constraints": [
      "2≤N≤202 \\le N \\le 202≤N≤20",
      "the sum of MMM over all polygons does not exceed 100100100",
      "∣x∣,∣y∣≤100|x|, |y| \\le 100∣x∣,∣y∣≤100",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (10 points):** N=2N = 2N=2 and both polygons are axis-aligned rectangles",
      "**Subtask #2 (20 points):** N=2N = 2N=2",
      "**Subtask #3 (20 points):** all polygons are axis-aligned rectangles",
      "Example Input`2",
      "4",
      "1 3",
      "2 2",
      "3 3",
      "2 4",
      "4",
      "0 0",
      "2 0",
      "2 2",
      "0 2",
      "`Example Output`3",
      "`Explanation**Example case 1:** Both P1P_1P1​ and P2P_2P2​ are squares. If we move P2P_2P2​ by 111 unit in the xxx-direction and by 222 units in the yyy-direction, the vertices of P1P_1P1​ become the midpoints of edges of P2P_2P2​."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer NNN. The descriptions of NNN polygons follow.\nFor each polygon:\n\nThe first line contains a single integer MMM denoting the number of its vertices.\nThe following MMM lines describe the vertices in counterclockwise order. Each of these lines contains two space-separated integers xxx and yyy denoting the coordinates of one vertex.",
    "outputFormat": "If it is impossible to make the polygons form a chain, print a single line containing the integer −1-1−1.\n\nOtherwise, print a single line containing one real number ― the minimum amount of time. Your answer will be considered correct if its absolute or relative error does not exceed 10−610^{-6}10−6.",
